/* cGridToCJGridBase.pkg

 Abstract base class for CJ grid conversion worker classes.
 Shared by:
   cDbGridTocDbCJGrid  (data-aware:     DbGrid/cTrDbGrid -> cDbCJGrid)
   cGridToCJGrid       (non-data-aware: Grid               -> cCJGrid)

 This class provides all transformation logic that operates at the cCJGrid level --
 property translation, legacy property removal, method renaming, Entry_Display
 commenting, and legacy-only method commenting.  It does NOT know about column
 sub-objects or Begin_Row / Entry_Item constructs; those are added by subclasses
 through three override hooks:

   OnGridStarted sGridIndent
       Called once when a matching grid declaration is detected.
       Subclasses reset their per-grid state here.

   OnHandleGridLine sLine sTrimLine sLower asOutput ByRef sGridIndent bSkip ByRef
       Called for every source line at nesting level 1 (direct grid content),
       before the base class's own property/method dispatch.
       Set bSkip True to consume the line; leave False to let base processing run.
       The subclass may emit content into asOutput before returning.

   OnBeforeGridEndObject asOutput ByRef sGridIndent
       Called once just before the grid's own End_Object is emitted.
       Subclasses flush any buffered column objects here.

 Shared transformations applied to each grid object found:
   - "Object X is a <OldGridClass>"    ->  "Object X is a <NewGridClass>"
   - Commented out: Set Main_File (hints which DDO to wire up)
   - Removed: Set Wrap_State, Set psColumnsID, Set Visible_State, Set Dynamic_Update_State
   - PRESERVED: Define <constant> N - preserved as-is since 2026-07-03 (was removed as a dead column-index
     constant, but preserved procedures still reference these; deleting broke the compile - see the
     pass-through branch in ProcessGridBody)
   - Removed: Set Child_Table_State, Set Item_Limit, Set Base_Item,
              Set pbComboNavigation, Set Move_Value_Out_State,
              Set Auto_Export_State, Set Auto_Index_State, Set Auto_Column_State
   - Commented out: Entry_Display procedure block
   - Translated: Set peResizeColumn        -> Set pbAllowColumnResize
   - Translated: Set Prompt_Button_Mode    -> Set pbHeaderPrompts
   - Translated: Set Allow_Top_Add_State   -> Set pbAllowAppendRow
   - Translated: Set Allow_Bottom_Add_State-> Set pbAllowAppendRow
   - Translated: Set Allow_Insert_Add_State-> Set pbAllowInsertRow
   - Translated: Set Auto_Save_State       -> Set pbAutoSave
   - Translated: Set Auto_Regenerate_State -> Set pbAutoRegenerate
   - Translated: Set No_Create_State       -> Set pbAllowAppendRow + Set pbAllowInsertRow (inverted)
   - Translated: Set No_Delete_State       -> Set pbAllowDeleteRow (inverted)
   - Translated: Set Read_Only_State       -> Set pbReadOnly
   - Translated: Set Header_Visible_State  -> Set pbShowHeader
   - Translated: Set Resize_Column_State   -> Set pbAllowColumnResize
   - Translated: Set Highlight_Row_State   -> Set pbShowRowFocus + Set pbSelectionEnable (a row shows its
                 colour, piHighlightBackColor, only when it can be selected; not on a dbList - see there)
   - Translated: Set Gridline_Mode         -> Set peHorizontalGridStyle / peVerticalGridStyle
   - Translated: Set CurrentRowColor       -> Set piHighlightBackColor
   - Translated: Set CurrentRowTextColor   -> Set piHighlightForeColor
   - Translated: Set CurrentCellColor      -> Set piFocusCellBackColor
   - Translated: Set CurrentCellTextColor  -> Set piFocusCellForeColor
   - Translated: Set Highlight_Row_Color   -> Set piHighlightBackColor   (CurrentRowColor's older name)
   - Translated: Set Current_Item_Color    -> Set piFocusCellBackColor   (CurrentCellColor's older name)
   - Translated: Set Select_Mode           -> Set pbMultipleSelection to True for Multi_Select, else removed
                 (dbGrid / dbList / List - the Grid converter maps it itself, the same way)
   - TODO:       Set Highlight_State       -> no cCJGrid counterpart; the TODO keeps the line

 Method override handling (Procedure/Function blocks inside the grid body):
   - Renamed:    Goto_Top_Row    -> MoveToFirstRow   (Forward Send/Get also renamed)
   - Renamed:    Goto_Bottom_Row -> MoveToLastRow     (Forward Send/Get also renamed)
   - Renamed:    Up_Row          -> MoveUpRow         (Forward Send/Get also renamed)
   - Renamed:    Down_Row        -> MoveDownRow       (Forward Send/Get also renamed)
   - Converted: Mouse_Click   Integer iWin Integer iPos  ->  Procedure OnRowDoubleClick Integer iRow Integer iCol
                (declaration replaced; Forward Send rewritten; old param names substituted in body)
   - Converted: Mouse_Down2  Integer iWin Integer iPos  ->  Procedure OnRowRightClick  Integer iRow Integer iCol
                (declaration replaced; Forward Send rewritten; old param names substituted in body)
   - Commented out with TODO hint: Fill_List, Refresh_Page, Request_New_Index, Move_to_Column
   - Commented out (no equivalent): Beginning_of_Data, End_of_Data, CheckBox_Item,
     Reorder_List, Auto_Reorder_List, Scroll, Clear_Current_Record, Col_Index, Display,
     DoCheckDisplayableRows, DoToggleColumnOrdering, Find_Current_Buffer, Find_Init,
     Find_Record, Find_RowId, ReadByRowId, Read_By_Recnum, ServerOrderingOverride,
     Activate_Column, Activate_Item, DoAdjustGridWidths, Column_Combo_*,
     DoMakeColumnVisible, Request_Superfind, SuperFind, SuperFind_Next,
     SuperFind_Previous, Validate_Items, Exec_Entry, Exec_Exit, Exec_Validate,
     Change_Row_Color (-> consider OnSetRowColor)
   - All other procedure/function overrides are preserved unchanged.

 All other content (other Set properties, nested objects, etc.) is preserved unchanged.

 The sParameter passed to TransformFiles must be a comma-separated string of 2 or 3
 class names:  "OldGridClass,NewGridClass[,NewColumnClass]"
 If sParameter is empty, the old class is detected by the subclass IsGridDeclaration
 override, and the default class names set in the subclass constructor are used.
*/

Use vWin32fh.pkg
Use RefactorConstants.h.pkg
Use GlobalFunctionsProcedures.pkg
Use cEncodingHelpers.pkg

#IFNDEF phoEditorRefactored
    Register_Function phoEditorRefactored Returns Handle
#ENDIF

Class cGridToCJGridBase is a cObject

    Procedure Construct_Object
        Forward Send Construct_Object
        Property String[]  pasSource
        Property String    psFileName          ""
        // Decline markers TransformSource added to the current file - a reason to write it back even when
        // nothing converted (see FileNeedsWrite). Reset per file at the top of TransformSource.
        Property Integer   piDeclineMarkers    0
        Property Integer   piChangedFiles       0
        Property Integer   piChangedGrids       0
        // Class name parameters (set by ParseAndSetParameter).
        // psLegacyGridClass: "" means pattern-based detection (defined by subclass).
        Property String    psLegacyGridClass   "DbGrid"
        Property String    psTargetGridClass   "cCJGrid"
        Property String    psTargetColumnClass "cCJGridColumn"
        /* AN EMPTY PARAMETER REACHES THE WORKSPACE'S SUBCLASSES (Nils 2026-09-05: "a legacy grid should be
           handled the same way as a legacy dbgrid, when no params are being specified"). psLegacyRootToken
           is the legacy root the Deep Scan learns subclasses under ("dbgrid" / "grid" / "dblist" / "list",
           set by each subclass constructor); pasLegacySubclasses is what the funclib knew for it when the
           parameter came in EMPTY (_LoadLegacySubclasses) - IsGridDeclaration takes those objects too, since
           2026-10-03 to leave them as they are (SubclassToLeave), not to convert them. A named parameter
           narrows the run to that one class, as before. */
        Property String    psLegacyRootToken   ""
        Property String[]  pasLegacySubclasses
        Property Boolean   pbEmptyParameter    False
        // The subclass objects an EMPTY run left as they are, per class (TallySubclassLeft) - one run note
        // per class at the end of the run (NoteSubclassesLeft), not one per object.
        Property String[]  pasSubclassLeftKeys
        Property String[]  pasSubclassLeftNames
        Property Integer[] paiSubclassLeftCounts
        // The DEDICATED legacy package whose sole purpose is the converted grid class,
        // safe to swap for the target package once every such object is converted
        // (dbGrid -> "Dftable.pkg", dbList -> "Dfsellst.pkg"). "" for Grid/List, whose
        // legacy class lives in the foundational Windows.pkg which must NEVER be removed
        // (only the target package is added for those). Set by the subclass constructor.
        // The TARGET package is not stored - it is derived from psTargetGridClass at
        // fix-up time via TargetUsePackageFor, so a user-supplied custom target class
        // (unknown package) automatically leaves the Use lines alone.
        Property String    psLegacyUsePackage  ""
        // Per-grid state: translatable Entry_Display properties collected during
        // grid pre-scan, flushed by FlushEntryDisplayExtracted before column objects.
        Property String[]  pasEntryDisplayExtracted
        Property Boolean   pbEntryDisplayFlushed  False
        Property Boolean   pbLastFileWasUtf8      False
        // Procedure-nesting depth captured at the CURRENT grid's declaration. > 0 means the
        // grid object is physically inside an open Procedure/Function body (e.g. a class's
        // Construct_Object). The subclasses read this to SUPPRESS any generated procedure
        // (LoadData/Activating/OnSetCalculatedValue) that would otherwise be nested inside
        // that procedure - illegal in DataFlex - and emit a //TODO instead (Nils 2026-06-11).
        Property Integer   piProcDepthAtGrid       0
    End_Procedure

    // *** File I/O ***

    // Reads a source file using the byte-safe helpers. Auto-detects UTF-8 BOM
    // and stores the result in pbLastFileWasUtf8 for use by WriteFile.
    Procedure ReadFile String sFileName
        String[] asSource
        Set psFileName        to sFileName
        Set pbLastFileWasUtf8 to (rfFileHasBOM(sFileName))
        Move (rfReadEncodedFileAsStringArray(sFileName)) to asSource
        Set pasSource to asSource
    End_Procedure

    // Writes the source array back to disk using the byte-safe helpers,
    // preserving the encoding (UTF-8 BOM or OEM/CP850) detected by ReadFile.
    Procedure WriteFile
        String   sFileName
        String[] asSource
        Boolean  bOK bIsUtf8

        Get psFileName        to sFileName
        Get pasSource         to asSource
        Get pbLastFileWasUtf8 to bIsUtf8
        // Through the write-time macro guard: macro code is never refactored (cRefactorFuncLib._GuardedWriteEncodedFile).
        Get _GuardedWriteEncodedFile of ghoFuncLib sFileName (&asSource) bIsUtf8 to bOK
        If (bOK = False) Begin
            Error DFERR_PROGRAM ("Write failed:" * sFileName * "(cGridToCJGridBase WriteFile)")
        End
    End_Procedure

    // *** Parameter parsing ***

    // Parses sParameter ("OldClass,NewGridClass[,NewColumnClass]") and sets the
    // three class name properties.
    // - Empty sParameter: use defaults set by the subclass constructor.
    // - 2 parts: exact old-class match and new grid class; column stays as-is.
    // - 3 parts: all three specified.
    // Returns False when sParameter is invalid, logging why - it does NOT raise an error.
    Function ParseAndSetParameter String sParameter Returns Boolean
        String[]  asParts
        String    sOld sNewGrid sNewCol sFn
        Integer   iParts

        Send _LoadLegacySubclasses sParameter
        // Empty -> leave defaults from constructor unchanged.
        If (sParameter = "") Begin
            Set psLegacyGridClass to ""
            Function_Return True
        End

        Move (StrSplitToArray(sParameter, ",")) to asParts
        Move (SizeOfArray(asParts)) to iParts

        If (iParts < 2 or iParts > 3) Begin
            /* A MALFORMED PARAMETER IS A CONFIGURATION STATE, NOT A PROGRAM FAULT
               (Nils 2026-08-03) - the same sweep as the two colliding-declaration converters
               in oRefactorFuncLib. `Error DFERR_PROGRAM` raises a RUNTIME error: a modal
               mid-run in the UI, and in a headless run an Error_Count entry that reads as an
               engine failure. Logged and skipped instead, so the user still learns why the
               converter did nothing. Guarded on ghoStatusLog - the DFUnit runner builds no
               engine, so there is no log to write to.

               The note is keyed on psExecutionContext, which the engine sets to the running
               function's name before each call - this base class serves all four converters
               (Grid, List, dbGrid, dbList) and cannot name itself, and hard-coding one of them
               would put a wrong name against the other three. */
            Get psExecutionContext of ghoFuncLib to sFn
            Send AddRunNote of ghoFuncLib sFn ('SKIPPED - the parameter must be "OldGridClass,NewGridClass[,NewColumnClass]".')
            Function_Return False
        End

        Move (Trim(asParts[0])) to sOld
        Move (Trim(asParts[1])) to sNewGrid

        If (sOld = "" or sNewGrid = "") Begin
            // Configuration state, not a fault - logged and skipped. See the note above.
            Get psExecutionContext of ghoFuncLib to sFn
            Send AddRunNote of ghoFuncLib sFn "SKIPPED - the old and new grid class names must both be given."
            Function_Return False
        End

        If (iParts = 3) Begin
            Move (Trim(asParts[2])) to sNewCol
        End
        If (sNewCol <> "") Begin
            Set psTargetColumnClass to sNewCol
        End

        // Store old class name as lowercase for case-insensitive comparison.
        Set psLegacyGridClass to (Lowercase(sOld))
        Set psTargetGridClass to sNewGrid
        Function_Return True
    End_Function

    // *** Use-statement fix-up ***

    // Maps a KNOWN standard target grid class to the package that defines it, so the
    // converter can add / swap the right "Use <pkg>". Returns "" for any class not in
    // the map - i.e. a user-supplied CUSTOM target class - so the fix-up then leaves
    // every Use line alone (we cannot know a custom class's package). Each standard
    // grid package pulls in its own column package (cCJGrid.pkg -> cCJGridColumn.pkg;
    // cDbCJGrid.pkg -> cCJGrid.pkg + cdbCJGridColumn.pkg; cDbCJGridPromptList.pkg ->
    // cDbCJGrid.pkg), so one Use of the grid package is self-sufficient.
    Function TargetUsePackageFor String sTargetClass Returns String
        String sLC
        Move (Lowercase(Trim(sTargetClass))) to sLC
        If (sLC = "ccjgrid") ;
            Function_Return "cCJGrid.pkg"
        If (sLC = "cdbcjgrid") ;
            Function_Return "cDbCJGrid.pkg"
        If (sLC = "cdbcjgridpromptlist") ;
            Function_Return "cDbCJGridPromptList.pkg"
        Function_Return ""
    End_Function

    // Returns the package a "Use <pkg>" directive names (the first token after "Use "),
    // or "" when sLine is not a Use directive (blank, a comment, or code). The "Use"
    // keyword match is case-insensitive; the returned name keeps its source casing. A
    // trailing // comment or extra tokens after the package name are ignored.
    Function UsePackageOnLine String sLine Returns String
        String  sTrim sRest
        Integer iPos

        Move (Trim(sLine)) to sTrim
        If (Lowercase(Left(sTrim, 4)) <> "use ") ;
            Function_Return ""
        // Everything after the "Use " keyword (positions 5..end).
        Move (Trim(Mid(sTrim, Length(sTrim), 5))) to sRest
        If (sRest = "") ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Pos(" ", sRest)) to iPos
        If (iPos > 0) ;
            Move (Left(sRest, (iPos - 1))) to sRest
        Move (Pos("//", sRest)) to iPos
        If (iPos > 0) ;
            Move (Left(sRest, (iPos - 1))) to sRest
        Function_Return (Trim(sRest))
    End_Function

    /* Does anything in the converted output still need the legacy package? Both the catalogue and
       the probe belong to ghoFuncLib, not here: cRefactorFuncLib._EnsureUsePackage has asked this
       exact question since the Edit -> cTextEdit converter dropped a Dftxtwin Use out from under an
       Import_Class_Protocol and cost a 388-error run. Its answer is the one to trust - it masks
       comments and literals and matches the class name ANYWHERE in real code, not just in an
       "is a" declaration, which is precisely how that one got through.

       So this is a two-line forwarder, and Dftable.pkg / Dfsellst.pkg are registered in that same
       canonical catalogue (_ClassesProvidedByPackage). An unregistered package yields an empty
       class list and reads as still needed, so its Use is left alone - the safe direction. */
    Function LegacyPackageStillUsed String[] ByRef asOutput String sLegacyPkg Returns Boolean
        Boolean  bStillUsed
        String[] asClasses
        Get _ClassesProvidedByPackage of ghoFuncLib sLegacyPkg to asClasses
        If (SizeOfArray(asClasses) = 0) ;
            Function_Return True
        Get _CodeNamesAnyClass of ghoFuncLib (&asOutput) asClasses to bStillUsed
        Function_Return bStillUsed
    End_Function

    // After a successful conversion, make sure the file "Use"s the package that defines
    // the NEW grid class - otherwise "Object X is a cDbCJGrid" is an undefined class and
    // will not compile. Called from TransformSource only when >= 1 grid was converted.
    //   - target package already Used  -> nothing added; a legacy Use that nothing needs
    //     any more is COMMENTED OUT (it is what keeps the compiler reporting an obsolete
    //     package for an already-converted file)
    //   - dedicated legacy package Used -> swapped IN PLACE to the target package,
    //     preserving its position + indentation (dbGrid's Dftable.pkg / dbList's
    //     Dfsellst.pkg; Grid/List's Windows.pkg is foundational, psLegacyUsePackage
    //     is "" for those, so it is never touched)
    //   - EITHER of those, but the package still defines a class the file declares
    //     (dbListRow is the live case) -> the legacy Use stays exactly as it is
    //   - neither present              -> the target Use is appended to the leading Use
    //     block (a file with no Use lines at all - a test fragment - is left alone)
    // A custom target class (TargetUsePackageFor = "") leaves every Use line untouched.
    Procedure FixUpUsePackage String[] ByRef asOutput
        String   sTargetClass sTargetPkg sLegacyPkg sUsed sTrim sIndent sCommented
        String[] asNew
        Integer  iCount iSize iLegacyIdx iLastUse iInsertAt iOut iUseDepth
        Boolean  bUseInBlock
        Boolean  bTargetPresent bSeenCode bInserted bLegacyStillUsed

        // Read the property into a local first - a bare property is not a valid
        // function argument (must be read via Get, or accessed function-style).
        Get psTargetGridClass to sTargetClass
        Get TargetUsePackageFor sTargetClass to sTargetPkg
        If (sTargetPkg = "") ;
            Procedure_Return
        Get psLegacyUsePackage to sLegacyPkg

        Move -1    to iLegacyIdx
        Move -1    to iLastUse
        Move False to bTargetPresent
        Move False to bSeenCode
        Move (SizeOfArray(asOutput) - 1) to iSize
        For iCount from 0 to iSize
            If (bSeenCode = False) ;
                Send rfUseAnchorStep asOutput[iCount] iCount (&iUseDepth) (&bUseInBlock) (&iLastUse)
            Get UsePackageOnLine asOutput[iCount] to sUsed
            If (sUsed <> "") Begin
                If (Lowercase(sUsed) = Lowercase(sTargetPkg)) ;
                    Move True to bTargetPresent
                If (sLegacyPkg <> "" and Lowercase(sUsed) = Lowercase(sLegacyPkg) and iLegacyIdx = -1) ;
                    Move iCount to iLegacyIdx
            End
            Else If (bSeenCode = False) Begin
                // First real code line ends the leading Use block, so a stray later Use
                // is not mistaken for a leading one. Skip blanks, // comments, /* ...
                // and # preprocessor lines (which legally sit among the Use statements).
                Move (Trim(asOutput[iCount])) to sTrim
                If (sTrim <> "" and Left(sTrim, 2) <> "//" and Left(sTrim, 2) <> "/*" and Left(sTrim, 1) <> "#") ;
                    Move True to bSeenCode
            End
        Loop

        /* Is the legacy package still earning its Use? Asked ONCE, and it governs both branches
           below - they are the same question with different answers available.

           It used to be asked in neither. The "target already present" branch simply left the
           legacy Use standing, on the reasoning that it was harmless; it is not. The compiler
           goes on reporting the obsolete package (4536) for a file whose grids all converted
           cleanly, which reads as "the refactoring did not work" and sends you looking for
           legacy classes that are no longer there (Nils 2026-08-10). And the swap branch removed
           the legacy Use unconditionally, which is the opposite hazard: a file that still
           declares a dbListRow loses the package that defines it and stops compiling. */
        Move False to bLegacyStillUsed
        If (sLegacyPkg <> "" and iLegacyIdx >= 0) ;
            Get LegacyPackageStillUsed (&asOutput) sLegacyPkg to bLegacyStillUsed

        /* Target package already Used. Nothing to add - but if the legacy Use is now dead weight,
           COMMENT IT OUT rather than delete it: the same reversible edit the converter makes to
           every legacy property it drops, so a reviewer diffing the file can see what went and
           put it back with two keystrokes if a build proves us wrong. */
        If (bTargetPresent = True) Begin
            // Via Get, not CommentOutLine(Self, ...): the function is defined further down this
            // class, and a function-style call has to be able to see its declaration already.
            If (sLegacyPkg <> "" and iLegacyIdx >= 0 and bLegacyStillUsed = False) Begin
                Get CommentOutLine asOutput[iLegacyIdx] to sCommented
                Move sCommented to asOutput[iLegacyIdx]
            End
            Procedure_Return
        End

        // Dedicated legacy Use present and nothing left that needs it: swap it in place for the
        // target package. Still needed -> leave it alone and fall through, so the target Use is
        // ADDED alongside it instead of replacing it.
        If (sLegacyPkg <> "" and iLegacyIdx >= 0 and bLegacyStillUsed = False) Begin
            Get GetIndent asOutput[iLegacyIdx] to sIndent
            Move (sIndent + "Use " + sTargetPkg) to asOutput[iLegacyIdx]
            Procedure_Return
        End

        // Neither present: append the target Use to the file's existing leading Use
        // block. A file with NO Use statements at all (only ever a synthetic test
        // fragment - real source that references the grid class already Uses some
        // package) is left alone rather than sprouting a lone Use at line 1.
        If (iLastUse < 0) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Move (iLastUse + 1) to iInsertAt
        Move False to bInserted
        Move 0 to iOut
        For iCount from 0 to iSize
            If (iCount = iInsertAt) Begin
                Move ("Use " + sTargetPkg) to asNew[iOut]
                Increment iOut
                Move True to bInserted
            End
            Move asOutput[iCount] to asNew[iOut]
            Increment iOut
        Loop
        If (bInserted = False) ;
            Move ("Use " + sTargetPkg) to asNew[iOut]
        Move asNew to asOutput
    End_Procedure

    /* WHAT A CONVERTED SUBCLASS OBJECT LEAVES BEHIND (Nils 2026-09-05, "tidy up those two listed things").
       An object declared through a subclass of the legacy class - "Object oX is a cEditGrid", named in the
       parameter (an EMPTY run leaves it as it is since 2026-10-03 - see SubclassToLeave) - is re-based on
       the target class like any other, and two
       things then hang loose: the subclass's own behaviour, which the target does not inherit, and the
       file's "Use <that subclass's package>", which nothing may need any more. The first gets a TODO
       as the object's first body line (SubclassMarkerLine) naming what it came from; the second is
       commented out (RetireConvertedSubclassUses) when the run's class index says the package defines
       nothing the file still names - a package may define more than the class it is named after, and
       only the file's own text can tell. Without an index (the DFUnit runner, a batch run) the Use
       stays: the safe direction, the same rule LegacyPackageStillUsed follows. */

    // The class token after the article of a declaration line, in its own casing; "" when none.
    Function LegacyClassOnLine String sTrimLine Returns String
        Integer iIsA iArt iPos
        String  sClass

        Get IsAArticlePos (Lowercase(sTrimLine)) (&iArt) to iIsA
        If (iIsA = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Trim(Mid(sTrimLine, CI_EOL, (iIsA + iArt)))) to sClass
        Move (Pos(" ", sClass)) to iPos
        If (iPos > 0) ;
            Move (Left(sClass, (iPos - 1))) to sClass
        Move (Pos("//", sClass)) to iPos
        If (iPos > 0) ;
            Move (Left(sClass, (iPos - 1))) to sClass
        Function_Return (Trim(sClass))
    End_Function

    // The plain legacy class of this converter's family, as written: dbGrid / Grid / dbList / List.
    Function PlainLegacyClassName Returns String
        String sToken
        Get psLegacyRootToken to sToken
        If (sToken = "dbgrid") ;
            Function_Return "dbGrid"
        If (sToken = "grid") ;
            Function_Return "Grid"
        If (sToken = "dblist") ;
            Function_Return "dbList"
        If (sToken = "list") ;
            Function_Return "List"
        Function_Return sToken
    End_Function

    // The TODO that opens a converted SUBCLASS object's body. Worded without the declaration itself
    // ("was a", never "is a"), so nothing scanning for object declarations trips over a comment.
    Function SubclassMarkerLine String sIndent String sObjName String sOldClass Returns String
        String sTarget
        Get psTargetGridClass to sTarget
        Function_Return (sIndent + "// TODO: " + sObjName + " was a " + sOldClass + " - a subclass of " + PlainLegacyClassName(Self) + " whose own behaviour this " + sTarget + " does not inherit; port it here, or subclass " + sTarget + " the same way.")
    End_Function

    // Every class one package file defines, per the run's class index - UPPERCASE, empty when unknown
    // or when no engine runs (the DFUnit runner). A test fixture overrides this with a fixed answer.
    Function ClassesOfPackage String sPkgLeaf Returns String[]
        String[] asOut
        If (ghoStatusLog = 0 or ghoFuncLib = 0) ;
            Function_Return asOut
        Get _ClassesDeclaredInPackage of ghoFuncLib sPkgLeaf to asOut
        Function_Return asOut
    End_Function

    // A copy of the file with every Use line blanked, for the probe below.
    Function _UseLinesBlanked String[] asLines Returns String[]
        String sUsed
        Integer i iSize
        Move (SizeOfArray(asLines) - 1) to iSize
        For i from 0 to iSize
            Get UsePackageOnLine asLines[i] to sUsed
            If (sUsed <> "") ;
                Move "" to asLines[i]
        Loop
        Function_Return asLines
    End_Function

    /* After the conversion: comment out a "Use <pkg>" whose file name is one of the converted subclasses
       (Use cEditGrid.pkg, once every cEditGrid object became a cCJGrid) - when the package defines
       nothing the file still names in code. The probe runs over a copy with every Use line blanked:
       the Use line itself names the class; comments and literals are masked by _CodeNamesAnyClass. */
    Procedure RetireConvertedSubclassUses String[] ByRef asOutput String[] asOldClasses
        String[] asProbe asClasses
        String   sUsed sLeaf sCommented
        Integer  i iSize iPos
        Boolean  bStill bProbeMade

        If (SizeOfArray(asOldClasses) = 0) ;
            Procedure_Return
        Move False to bProbeMade
        Move (SizeOfArray(asOutput) - 1) to iSize
        For i from 0 to iSize
            Get UsePackageOnLine asOutput[i] to sUsed
            If (sUsed <> "") Begin
                Move (Lowercase(sUsed)) to sLeaf
                Move (RightPos("\", sLeaf)) to iPos
                If (iPos > 0) ;
                    Move (Right(sLeaf, (Length(sLeaf) - iPos))) to sLeaf
                Move (RightPos(".", sLeaf)) to iPos
                If (iPos > 1) ;
                    Move (Left(sLeaf, (iPos - 1))) to sLeaf
                If (SearchArray(sLeaf, asOldClasses) <> -1) Begin
                    Get ClassesOfPackage sUsed to asClasses
                    If (SizeOfArray(asClasses) > 0) Begin
                        If (bProbeMade = False) Begin
                            Get _UseLinesBlanked asOutput to asProbe
                            Move True to bProbeMade
                        End
                        Get _CodeNamesAnyClass of ghoFuncLib (&asProbe) asClasses to bStill
                        If (bStill = False) Begin
                            Get CommentOutLine asOutput[i] to sCommented
                            Move sCommented to asOutput[i]
                        End
                    End
                End
            End
        Loop
    End_Procedure

    // *** Detection helpers ***

    // Position + length of the declaration ARTICLE (" is a " / " is an ") in sLowLine. Legacy
    // DataFlex accepts BOTH articles ('Object text_formatter is an edit' - WinServ 2026-07-17,
    // natural English before a vowel-initial class; the class-names PARAMETER admits vowel-initial
    // user subclasses everywhere), so every declaration matcher and splice must too. Returns the
    // article's start position (0 = neither present); iArtLen ByRef = 6 for " is a ", 7 for
    // " is an " - the class token starts iArtLen chars after the position.
    Function IsAArticlePos String sLowLine Integer ByRef iArtLen Returns Integer
        Integer iPos
        Move (Pos(" is a ", sLowLine)) to iPos
        Move 6 to iArtLen
        If (iPos = 0) Begin
            Move (Pos(" is an ", sLowLine)) to iPos
            Move 7 to iArtLen
        End
        Function_Return iPos
    End_Function

    /* The subclasses an EMPTY parameter reaches, asked from the funclib - which the FT deep-scan driver
       feeds with the "Class X is a <legacy>" pairs of the last scan (cBaseFuncLib.LearnedSubclassesOf). A
       named parameter narrows the run to that class: the list is cleared. Called at the top of the base
       ParseAndSetParameter, and by the Grid / List / dbList overrides' empty branch, which returns before
       the base runs. */
    Procedure _LoadLegacySubclasses String sParameter
        String[] asSubs

        Set pbEmptyParameter to (sParameter = "")
        If (sParameter = "" and ghoFuncLib <> 0 and psLegacyRootToken(Self) <> "") ;
            Get LearnedSubclassesOf of ghoFuncLib (psLegacyRootToken(Self)) to asSubs
        Set pasLegacySubclasses to asSubs
    End_Procedure

    // Is sClassNameLc (lowercase) one of the subclasses the EMPTY parameter reaches? False after a named one.
    Function IsLearnedLegacySubclass String sClassNameLc Returns Boolean
        String[] asSubs

        If (pbEmptyParameter(Self) = False) ;
            Function_Return False
        Get pasLegacySubclasses to asSubs
        Function_Return (SearchArray(Lowercase(Trim(sClassNameLc)), asSubs) <> -1)
    End_Function

    /* A SUBCLASS OBJECT STAYS AS IT IS UNDER AN EMPTY PARAMETER (Nils 2026-10-03: "a subclass can't be
       blindly swapped for a CodeJock grid class without first have converted the cEntryGrid subclass").
       Until then an EMPTY run re-based such an object on the plain target class, with a TODO for what the
       subclass added - and what a subclass adds is real behaviour: one workspace's MyDbGrid anchors the
       grid and translates its labels, its cEntryGrid binds keys to row methods of its own. The swap lost
       all of it in 2,126 objects across 1,142 files, and the program still compiled, except where it
       called a method of the subclass. The dbList converter had refused this from the start (Nils
       2026-07-03 - see RefactorDbListTocDbCJGridPromptList), until the empty parameter was widened on
       2026-09-05.

       So an EMPTY run converts the plain legacy class only. An object of any other class it detects - a
       subclass the Deep Scan learned, or for dbGrid / dbList a name that ends in the token - passes
       through as it is, and is counted for the run note. A NAMED parameter still converts the class it
       names: that is how the objects follow once the subclass is ported - "MyDbGrid,AmDbCJGrid,
       cDbCJGridColumn" re-bases them on the ported class. Returns the class to leave, "" to convert. */
    Function SubclassToLeave String sTrimLine Returns String
        String sOldClass

        If (pbEmptyParameter(Self) = False) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Get LegacyClassOnLine sTrimLine to sOldClass
        If (sOldClass = "" or Lowercase(sOldClass) = psLegacyRootToken(Self)) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Function_Return sOldClass
    End_Function

    /* Why the objects of sClass were left, and what to do instead - the end of its run note. A dbGrid, Grid
       or dbList subclass has a converter of its own since 2026-10-04 - ConvertGridSubclassToCodeJock ports
       the class in place and converts its objects with it; a List subclass is still ported by hand. */
    Function SubclassLeftReason String sClass Returns String
        String sTarget sWhy
        Get psTargetGridClass to sTarget
        Move ("a workspace subclass of " + PlainLegacyClassName(Self) + ", and a plain " + sTarget + " would lose what it adds.") to sWhy
        If (psLegacyRootToken(Self) = "list") ;
            Function_Return (sWhy + " Port " + sClass + " to a class based on " + sTarget + " first, then convert these objects with the parameter '" + sClass + ",<the new class>," + psTargetColumnClass(Self) + "'.")
        Function_Return (sWhy + " Run ConvertGridSubclassToCodeJock with the parameter '" + sClass + "': it ports " + sClass + " to " + sTarget + " in place and converts these objects with it, or says in its run notes why it cannot.")
    End_Function

    // Counts one object of sClass that SubclassToLeave left as it is.
    Procedure TallySubclassLeft String sClass
        String[]  asKeys asNames
        Integer[] aiCounts
        Integer   iAt

        Get pasSubclassLeftKeys   to asKeys
        Get pasSubclassLeftNames  to asNames
        Get paiSubclassLeftCounts to aiCounts
        Move (SearchArray(Lowercase(sClass), asKeys)) to iAt
        If (iAt = -1) Begin
            Move (Lowercase(sClass)) to asKeys[-1]
            Move sClass              to asNames[-1]
            Move 1                   to aiCounts[-1]
        End
        Else ;
            Move (aiCounts[iAt] + 1) to aiCounts[iAt]
        Set pasSubclassLeftKeys   to asKeys
        Set pasSubclassLeftNames  to asNames
        Set paiSubclassLeftCounts to aiCounts
    End_Procedure

    Procedure _ClearSubclassesLeft
        String[]  asNone
        Integer[] aiNone
        Set pasSubclassLeftKeys   to asNone
        Set pasSubclassLeftNames  to asNone
        Set paiSubclassLeftCounts to aiNone
    End_Procedure

    /* One run note per subclass whose objects the run left as they are, then the tally starts over. Keyed
       on the running function (psExecutionContext), as NoteDeclinedGrid is; outside a run there is no
       function to note into. */
    Procedure NoteSubclassesLeft
        String[]  asNames
        Integer[] aiCounts
        String    sFn
        Integer   i iLast

        Get psExecutionContext of ghoFuncLib to sFn
        Get pasSubclassLeftNames  to asNames
        Get paiSubclassLeftCounts to aiCounts
        If (Trim(sFn) <> "") Begin
            Move (SizeOfArray(asNames) - 1) to iLast
            For i from 0 to iLast
                Send AddRunNote of ghoFuncLib sFn (String(aiCounts[i]) + " object(s) of " + asNames[i] + " left as they are - " + (SubclassLeftReason(Self, asNames[i])))
            Loop
        End
        Send _ClearSubclassesLeft
    End_Procedure

    // Override in subclasses to detect the specific legacy grid class.
    // When psLegacyGridClass is set, should do an exact (case-insensitive) match.
    // When psLegacyGridClass is empty, should fall back to a pattern check - and take the
    // learned subclasses too (IsLearnedLegacySubclass), as all four overrides do.
    // Base implementation always returns False.
    Function IsGridDeclaration String sTrimLower Returns Boolean
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    // Returns True when sTrimLower is an Object declaration of any kind (either article).
    Function IsObjectDeclaration String sTrimLower Returns Boolean
        Integer iIsA iArt
        If (Pos("object ", sTrimLower) <> 1) ;
            Function_Return False
        Get IsAArticlePos sTrimLower (&iArt) to iIsA
        Function_Return (iIsA <> 0)
    End_Function

    // The class name an Object declaration names - lowercase, as sTrimLower is - or "" when sTrimLower is no
    // Object declaration: "object ox is a cdbcjgrid { ... }" gives "cdbcjgrid". Either article ("is a" /
    // "is an" - see IsAArticlePos); anything after a space (metadata tags) is dropped. The shared head of
    // every IsGridDeclaration override.
    Function DeclaredClassName String sTrimLower Returns String
        Integer iIsA iArt
        String  sClassName

        If (Pos("object ", sTrimLower) <> 1) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Get IsAArticlePos sTrimLower (&iArt) to iIsA
        If (iIsA = 0) ;
            Function_Return ""
        Move (Trim(Mid(sTrimLower, CI_EOL, (iIsA + iArt)))) to sClassName
        Move (Pos(CS_S, sClassName)) to iIsA
        If (iIsA > 0) ;
            Move (Left(sClassName, iIsA - 1)) to sClassName
        Function_Return sClassName
    End_Function

    // Returns True when sTrimLower is an Entry_Display procedure start.
    Function IsEntryDisplayProcedure String sTrimLower Returns Boolean
        Function_Return (Pos("procedure ", sTrimLower) = 1 and Pos("entry_display", sTrimLower) <> 0)
    End_Function

    // Returns True when sTrimLower is a legacy grid-only Set property to remove.
    Function IsLegacyGridProperty String sTrimLower Returns Boolean
        If (Left(sTrimLower, 4) <> "set ") Begin
            Function_Return False
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "wrap_state") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "pscolumnsid") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "child_table_state") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "item_limit") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "base_item") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "pbcombonavigation") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "move_value_out_state") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "auto_export_state") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "auto_index_state") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "auto_column_state") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "visible_state") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "dynamic_update_state") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    // Returns True when sTrimLower is a legacy grid Set property that should be
    // commented out rather than removed, so the programmer retains it as a hint.
    //   Set Main_File - tells the programmer which DDO to wire up on the new grid.
    Function IsCommentOutGridProperty String sTrimLower Returns Boolean
        If (Left(sTrimLower, 4) <> "set ") Begin
            Function_Return False
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "main_file") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        /* The embedded-prompt pair. Both DO have counterparts - Prompt_Button_Value and
           Prompt_Button_Mode, declared in cCJGridColumn.pkg with the same "..." default - but they
           live on the COLUMN, while the legacy properties sit on the GRID. That change of scope is
           why this is a comment-out and not a rename: the value would have to be pushed into every
           column object, which this line-level pass cannot do safely. Left unhandled they were
           copied through verbatim into the converted object, where they do not compile (Nils
           2026-08-04). LegacyOnlyGridPropertyHint names the counterpart. */
        If (sTrimLower contains "psembeddedbuttonvalue") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        If (sTrimLower contains "pbembeddedprompts") Begin
            Function_Return True
        End
        Function_Return False
    End_Function

    /* The closest cCJGrid equivalent of a legacy grid PROPERTY, or "" when there is none.
       Mirrors LegacyOnlyGridMethodHint on the method side, so a commented-out property carries the
       same actionable note a commented-out call does. */
    Function LegacyOnlyGridPropertyHint String sTrimLower Returns String
        If (sTrimLower contains "psembeddedbuttonvalue") ;
            Function_Return "Prompt_Button_Value on the COLUMN object (cCJGridColumn), not on the grid"
        If (sTrimLower contains "pbembeddedprompts") ;
            Function_Return "Prompt_Button_Mode on the COLUMN object (PB_PromptAuto / PB_PromptOn / PB_PromptOff)"
        Function_Return ""
    End_Function

    // Returns the leading whitespace of sLine (spaces / tabs), preserving exact
    // characters.  Used by all conversion helpers that need to mirror the source
    // line's indent into a synthesised output line.
    //
    // IMPORTANT: must use LTrim (leading-only) rather than Trim (both ends), because
    // a source line that has trailing whitespace would otherwise compute an indent
    // length that is too large -- the "Left(sLine, N)" call would then grab part of
    // the actual content as "indent", corrupting the synthesised output.
    // Example bug: "    If (cond) cmd    " trimmed gives 49 chars, full length 57,
    //              difference 8, Left(sLine, 8) = "    If (" instead of "    ".
    Function GetIndent String sLine Returns String
        Function_Return (Left(sLine, (Length(sLine) - Length(LTrim(sLine)))))
    End_Function

    // Returns the line commented out with the '//' at COLUMN 1 and the original line - indentation
    // included - preserved verbatim after it (Nils 2026-07-05: the old indent-then-'//' style
    // scattered the markers across a commented block and made a commented Entry_Display read
    // ragged). Uncommenting a block is then a uniform strip of the two leading chars; an
    // already-commented line simply gains a second marker at the front ('//// ...').
    // Example: "    Set Main_File to Orders" -> "//    Set Main_File to Orders"
    Function CommentOutLine String sLine Returns String
        Function_Return ("//" + sLine)
    End_Function

    // Extracts the method name (second word) from a trimmed-lowercase procedure or
    // function declaration line.  Returns "" when the line is not a declaration.
    Function ParseProcFuncName String sTrimLower Returns String
        Integer iStart iSpace
        String  sRest

        If (Left(sTrimLower, 10) = "procedure ") Begin
            Move 11 to iStart
        End
        Else If (Left(sTrimLower, 9) = "function ") Begin
            Move 10 to iStart
        End
        Else Begin
            Function_Return ""
        End
        Move (Trim(Mid(sTrimLower, CI_EOL, iStart))) to sRest
        Move (Pos(CS_S, sRest)) to iSpace
        If (iSpace > 0) Begin
            Function_Return (Left(sRest, iSpace - 1))
        End
        Function_Return sRest
    End_Function

    // Case-insensitive replacement of sOldLower (already lowercase) with sNewName
    // in sLine.  Finds the first occurrence only.
    Function ReplaceMethodName String sLine String sOldLower String sNewName Returns String
        Integer iPos iLen
        String  sLower

        Move (Lowercase(sLine)) to sLower
        Move (Pos(sOldLower, sLower)) to iPos
        If (iPos = 0) Begin
            Function_Return sLine
        End
        Move (Length(sOldLower)) to iLen
        Function_Return (Left(sLine, iPos - 1) + sNewName + Mid(sLine, CI_EOL, iPos + iLen))
    End_Function

    /* Rename ONE identifier - a converted Mouse_Click / Mouse_Down2 PARAMETER - everywhere on a body
       line, as a WHOLE WORD, case-insensitively, outside string literals and comments, keeping the
       rest of the line as typed. ReplaceMethodName above (a bare substring, first hit only) is right
       for a method NAME on a Send/Forward line, but it was also used for these parameters - and a
       legacy 'Procedure mouse_click Integer window Integer char_pos' body carrying
       'Send SafeCloseView (Jobbreg_MultiWindow(Self))' came out as 'Jobbreg_MultiiRow(Self)' =
       E 4328 undefined symbol, twice (WinServ PROJECT.vw, Nils 2026-08-17: the error count went UP
       after the run). Boundaries: a non-identifier char - or the line's ends - on both sides
       (_IsIdentifierChar's rule: letters, digits, '_'); a name inside "..." / '...' or after '//' is
       data and is left alone. Every occurrence on the line, not just the first. */
    Function ReplaceParamName String sLine String sOldName String sNewName Returns String
        String sMask sLow sOldLow sCh sQuote
        Integer i iLen iOldLen iPos iStart
        Boolean bBefore bAfter

        Move (Trim(sOldName)) to sOldName
        If (sOldName = "" or sLine = "") ;
            Function_Return sLine
        // A position-aligned mask: string literal content and any // comment become spaces, so a
        // hit can only land in code. DataFlex has no escape inside a literal - a quote of the same
        // kind closes it.
        Move sLine to sMask
        Move (Length(sLine)) to iLen
        Move "" to sQuote
        Move 1 to i
        While (i <= iLen)
            Move (Mid(sLine, 1, i)) to sCh
            If (sQuote <> "") Begin
                If (sCh = sQuote) ;
                    Move "" to sQuote
                Else ;
                    Move (Overstrike(" ", sMask, i)) to sMask
            End
            Else If (sCh = '"' or sCh = "'") Begin
                Move sCh to sQuote
            End
            Else If (sCh = "/" and i < iLen) Begin
                If (Mid(sLine, 1, i + 1) = "/") Begin
                    Move (Left(sMask, i - 1) + Repeat(" ", iLen - i + 1)) to sMask
                    Move iLen to i                      // the rest is comment - stop
                End
            End
            Increment i
        Loop
        Move (Lowercase(sMask))    to sLow
        Move (Lowercase(sOldName)) to sOldLow
        Move (Length(sOldName))    to iOldLen
        Move 1 to iStart
        Repeat
            Move 0 to iPos
            If (iStart <= Length(sLow) - iOldLen + 1) ;
                Move (Pos(sOldLow, sLow, iStart)) to iPos
            If (iPos > 0) Begin
                Move (iPos > 1 and _IsIdentifierChar(ghoFuncLib, Mid(sLow, 1, iPos - 1)))              to bBefore
                Move ((iPos + iOldLen <= Length(sLow)) and _IsIdentifierChar(ghoFuncLib, Mid(sLow, 1, iPos + iOldLen))) to bAfter
                If (bBefore = False and bAfter = False) Begin
                    // Splice the RAW line and re-mask the same span in the mask, so later
                    // positions stay aligned with the line.
                    Move (Left(sLine, iPos - 1) + sNewName + Mid(sLine, CI_EOL, iPos + iOldLen)) to sLine
                    Move (Left(sLow,  iPos - 1) + Lowercase(sNewName) + Mid(sLow,  CI_EOL, iPos + iOldLen)) to sLow
                    Move (iPos + Length(sNewName)) to iStart
                End
                Else ;
                    Move (iPos + 1) to iStart
            End
        Until (iPos = 0)
        Function_Return sLine
    End_Function

    // Returns the cDbCJGrid replacement name for a legacy grid method that has a
    // clean 1-to-1 rename, or "" when the method is not in the rename list.
    Function RenameGridMethod String sMethodLower Returns String
        If (sMethodLower = "goto_top_row") Begin
            Function_Return "MoveToFirstRow"
        End
        If (sMethodLower = "goto_bottom_row") Begin
            Function_Return "MoveToLastRow"
        End
        If (sMethodLower = "up_row") Begin
            Function_Return "MoveUpRow"
        End
        If (sMethodLower = "down_row") Begin
            Function_Return "MoveDownRow"
        End
        // Self-rename: preserves the procedure name as-is but routes the body
        // through bInRenameProcedure so it is emitted unchanged by the base class
        // (bypassing subclass transformations such as the bare-Send comment-out rule).
        If (sMethodLower = "activating") Begin
            Function_Return "Activating"
        End
        Function_Return ""
    End_Function

    // Returns True when sMethodLower is a legacy grid method that does not exist
    // in cCJGrid (or whose behaviour differs enough that it must be reviewed).
    // The four clean-rename methods are NOT included here.
    Function IsLegacyOnlyGridMethod String sMethodLower Returns Boolean
        If (sMethodLower = "beginning_of_data") Begin
            Function_Return True
